@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# OpenClaw snapshot identity and fast-uri repairs
+
+This derived package keeps the `chrome-devtools-mcp@1.8.0` public manifest and
+entry contracts. It is not the unmodified published npm artifact.
+
+The original npm 1.8.0 tarball has integrity
+`sha512-Wrm9z0/5WbVs778apjWgYRkpe9bvYQWjK2zVRwqoPAtz1IHQ5+GvotM07UGXJcfrA0rj6Gt1Pnn5+w/Tf1nU4w==`.
+That integrity and its upstream provenance apply only to the original bytes,
+not this derived artifact.
+
+## Snapshot Identity Backport
+
+The reviewed upstream source is commit
+`06c8d4bc44f68bde8bd3fcd97dcc47375df81fe9`, from
+https://github.com/ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp/pull/2788.
+
+- `TextSnapshot.js` retains OpenClaw's reviewed snapshot-owner implementation.
+- `McpPage.js` supplies the known element frame for DOM-result reverse lookup.
+- `third_party/index.js` exports its already-bundled `CdpFrame` class.
+
+The TextSnapshot and McpPage bytes are identical to the existing OpenClaw
+snapshot patch. The complete snapshot repair remains in place.
+
+## Reproducible Main Bundle Repair
+
+The main bundle is rebuilt from Chrome source
+`45f187b1e3202c9f32ddba913be5d68751c3caa3` and DevTools gitlink
+`6fdb53e0f7a5cb1ebf16e40c45439a5c8007d9be`, with the sole build-lock dependency
+substitution `fast-uri@3.1.5` to `fast-uri@3.1.8`.
+
+Derived build-lock SHA-256:
+`1fbe9c1958de13a7a1d51d252d57299a80e06a6a42b3c8e3c1b633ca3448dfd9`.
+Two clean isolated source trees use Node 26.9.0, npm 11.19.1, macOS 26.6.2 arm64,
+hooks-disabled offline installation, and a network-denied build. The build
+receipt, exact inputs, executable recipe, output hashes and regression evidence
+are retained with the OpenClaw 2026.9.6 Chrome remediation review artifacts.
+No upstream SLSA attestation is claimed for the rebuilt bytes.
+
+The original `LICENSE` remains unchanged. `third_party/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`
+updates only the fast-uri component version from 3.1.5 to 3.1.8.
+
+## Lighthouse Residual
+
+The shipped Lighthouse bundle remains byte-identical. Its committed source blob
+is `8b7eb8c6c7ce927ba29931a0740858d633b884a0`; no source commit is invented for
+the separately generated Lighthouse input.
+
+Its retained lodash-es 4.17.21 subset still has component-version findings
+`GHSA-r5fr-rjxr-66jc` (high), `GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg` (moderate), and
+`GHSA-f23m-r3pf-42rh` (moderate). The inspected subset lacks the affected
+template/unset/omit implementations. These are content-bound residuals, not a
+package-level lodash upgrade or a blanket advisory-clean claim.
+
+Remove or supersede these local repairs only after a reviewed upstream artifact
+preserves the same snapshot, stdio, schema and URI regression contracts.
